{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest v2 PDP — the §3.5 image-index RESOLVER. One place decides which product image a slot gets,
  and it can never hand back a slide with baked-in marketing text (WINNING-SPEC §3.6 never-use list +
  PDP BRIEF §6 per-product bans).

  Usage — the snippet PRINTS one integer: the 0-based index into product.images. Capture it, then take
  the image object (and let a merchant image_picker override win, exactly as §3.5 writes it):

      {%- capture env2_i -%}{%- render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-image', product: product, slot: 'hero', index: section.settings.hero_image_index -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign env2_i = env2_i | plus: 0 -%}
      {%- assign hero = section.settings.hero_image | default: product.images[env2_i] | default: product.featured_image -%}

  Inputs
    product : required. Anything else prints 0.
    slot    : hero | context | close | card | wall-pair | big | small | thumb | ask   (default 'hero')
    index   : the section's 1-based range setting (1 = admin position 1 = product.images[0]).
              0 / blank / nil  -> the per-product ledger default for the slot.
    fallback: optional 0-based index used when the ledger has nothing for this handle.
    emit    : 'no_clean' -> print '1' or '0' INSTEAD of an index and stop: does this handle have NO
              text-free photograph at any index at all (collection WINNING-SPEC §3.6.2)? Opt-in, so
              every existing caller is untouched.
    glyph   : true -> print the literal string 'glyph' instead of an index for such a handle, so one
              call answers both questions. Opt-in for the same reason. A caller that does not pass it
              gets exactly the index it got before this parameter existed.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ the glyph branch (collection §3.6.2)
  ADDITIVE, 2026-09-03, by the collection plumbing engineer. Contact sheets over brief/assets/img/,
  indexes 0-3, all 27 products: FIFTEEN handles have no text-free image at ANY index. Every one is a
  marketing poster — baked Hebrew headline, spec icon strip, cream or beige ground — and §6.10 bans
  cream on any surface, including a photograph's own ground. modern-led-bollard-light-5w-ip65 also
  carries three conflicting third-party wordmarks (LUMIERE / LUMORA / LUMIRA) across four images.

  The PDP's "silently step to index 1" resolver is not enough there: it can only choose a different
  poster. So this snippet now also ANSWERS the question, and the collection page draws the lamp instead
  (snippets/elmsnest-v2-coll-glyph.liquid, the plate captioned "איור · אין תצלום נקי").

  The stepping behaviour is UNCHANGED for every existing caller: the PDP asks for an index and still
  gets the same index it got before. Only a caller that passes emit:'no_clean' or glyph:true sees the
  new answer. A product with no images at all also answers '1' — there is nothing to render but a plate.

  Guarantees
    1. The printed index is always inside 0 … product.images.size-1 (0 when there are no images).
    2. It is never a banned index for that handle. If the requested one is banned, the resolver steps
       to the next allowed index (wrapping from 0), silently — no log, the right picture.
    3. An image_picker override is the merchant's own file and is NOT filtered: it is applied by the
       caller, after this snippet.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign env2_n = 0
  if product != blank
    assign env2_n = product.images.size
  endif

  comment
    Collection WINNING-SPEC §3.6.2 — the handles with NO clean frame at any index 0-3, so no
    index can be stepped to. Five spot products (the whole ספוטים collection except dual-head), five
    path products, the bollard with the three wordmarks, two decor posters on cream, and two wall
    products that are posters or white studio cut-outs. Fifteen handles, listed there in one table,
    plus solar-rope-string-lights (see the ledger note below) — sixteen.
  endcomment
  assign env2_no_clean_image = '|solar-security-light-100-led|solar-garden-lantern-9-led|rechargeable-telescopic-camping-lantern|solar-floodlight-ip67-remote-timer|solar-garden-spotlight-52-led|warm-solar-step-deck-lights|waterproof-solar-deck-step-lights|retro-solar-path-lights-set|modern-solar-path-lights-set|swaying-solar-path-lights-ip65|modern-led-bollard-light-5w-ip65|led-globe-string-lights|decorative-led-net-lights|magnetic-rechargeable-touch-wall-light|solar-wall-light-motion-sensor-ip65|solar-rope-string-lights|'
  assign env2_nc = '0'
  if env2_n == 0
    assign env2_nc = '1'
  endif
  if product != blank
    assign env2_nckey = '|' | append: product.handle | append: '|'
    if env2_no_clean_image contains env2_nckey
      assign env2_nc = '1'
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- if emit == 'no_clean' -%}{{ env2_nc }}{%- elsif glyph == true and env2_nc == '1' -%}glyph{%- elsif env2_n == 0 -%}0{%- else -%}
{%- liquid
  assign env2_slot = slot | default: 'hero'

  comment
    Per-product slot ledger (§3.5 "Defaults that ship"). 0-based; admin position = value + 1.
    Format: |<handle>:,<slot>=<i>,…,|   — the commas make every key ",slot=" so no key is a prefix of another.

    Extended 2026-09-02 (additive, by the §4.8 related engineer, proved against the live CDN images):
    four more handles carry baked-in marketing text at index 0, which is where the "any other product"
    default for the card/close slots would have landed. Their first text-free frame is recorded here so
    every section — and round 2's catalogue card — gets a real photograph:
      modern-led-wall-light-indoor-outdoor  0 = "עיצוב מודרני…" slide, 1/2/3 = specs/labels → 4 is clean
      solar-firefly-garden-lights           0 = 4-up with a caption, 1 = diagram              → 3 is clean
      solar-edison-string-lights            0 = "עמיד וחזק", 1 = "מידות ומפרט"                → 3 is clean
      powerful-solar-garden-light           0/1/3 carry a caption chip, 4/5 are diagrams          → 2 is clean
    solar-rope-string-lights has NO text-free frame at all: 0/1/3/4 carry a headline, 5 is a diagram,
    and 2 carries an "עמידות IP65" chip that only a top crop removes; brief/WINNING-SPEC §3.6 uses it
    with object-position 50% 100%. A card cannot crop, so no row is recorded for it here — and since a
    card cannot crop, 2026-09-03 (integration) moved it into env2_no_clean_image as well, after the
    deployed decor page shipped its index-0 headline poster as a card thumbnail. The PDP is unaffected:
    emit:'no_clean' and glyph:true are opt-in and no PDP section passes either.

    'context' rows, added 2026-09-03 (integration): the collection's band scene photograph asks for the
    context slot, and only sections/elmsnest-v2-coll-bands.liquid ever does, so these rows cannot reach
    the PDP. Without them the slot fell to the catalogue default 0, which is a baked-headline poster for
    fireflies ("מראה קסום בגינה", shipped in the decor wide band), for indoor-outdoor, for edison and
    for powerful. Each row carries the same clean index its card row already names.

    Extended again for the CLOSING screen (§4.7's full-bleed photograph): the "ask" slot is deliberately
    NOT the hero's own frame, so the page does not open and close on the same picture. A = the lit
    crystal balls in the tree (0), B = the bollard on the path at night (1), C = the lamp on the wall (3),
    which is the only night-lit frame that product owns.
  endcomment
  assign env2_led = '|solar-crystal-ball-string-lights:,hero=2,context=2,close=0,card=0,big=2,small=0,thumb=0,wall-pair=2,ask=0,|stainless-steel-solar-path-light-ip65:,hero=0,context=3,close=3,card=0,big=3,small=1,thumb=3,wall-pair=3,ask=1,|waterproof-led-wall-light-ip65-6w-12w:,hero=1,context=3,close=1,card=1,big=3,small=1,thumb=1,wall-pair=3,ask=3,|modern-led-wall-light-indoor-outdoor:,card=4,close=4,context=4,|solar-firefly-garden-lights:,card=3,close=3,context=3,|solar-edison-string-lights:,card=3,close=3,context=3,|powerful-solar-garden-light:,card=2,close=2,context=2,|'

  comment
    Banned indices. The 15 handles of brief/WINNING-SPEC.md §3.6 (index 0 carries baked-in text; for
    dual-head-garden-light-10w-ip65 it is images 1–3 that carry it and index 0 that is clean), plus the
    three archetypes' per-image bans from the PDP BRIEF §6 ledger:
      A solar-crystal-ball-string-lights   1 = "22 מטר / 200 LED" slide, 3 = installation infographic
      B stainless-steel-solar-path-light   2 = dimensions slide
      C waterproof-led-wall-light-6w-12w   0 = slogan slide, 2 = a supplier 2x2 contact sheet (four equal
                                          cells, black/white x two shapes, on a white seamless) — it was
                                          the "small" gallery frame and §6.2 forbids four equal cells in
                                          a row, so it is banned from every slot and small falls to 1
  endcomment
  assign env2_deny = '|retro-solar-path-lights-set=,0,|warm-solar-step-deck-lights=,0,|waterproof-solar-deck-step-lights=,0,|solar-garden-lantern-9-led=,0,|solar-garden-spotlight-52-led=,0,|solar-security-light-100-led=,0,|modern-solar-path-lights-set=,0,|solar-floodlight-ip67-remote-timer=,0,|decorative-led-net-lights=,0,|led-globe-string-lights=,0,|modern-led-bollard-light-5w-ip65=,0,|rechargeable-telescopic-camping-lantern=,0,|swaying-solar-path-lights-ip65=,0,|magnetic-rechargeable-touch-wall-light=,0,|dual-head-garden-light-10w-ip65=,1,2,3,|solar-crystal-ball-string-lights=,1,3,|stainless-steel-solar-path-light-ip65=,2,|waterproof-led-wall-light-ip65-6w-12w=,0,2,|'

  # 1. the wanted index: the section setting (1-based) wins, else the ledger, else the fallback
  assign env2_i = -1
  assign env2_want = index | default: 0 | plus: 0
  if env2_want > 0
    assign env2_i = env2_want | minus: 1
  endif
  if env2_i < 0
    assign env2_lkey = '|' | append: product.handle | append: ':'
    assign env2_lrow = env2_led | split: env2_lkey
    if env2_lrow.size > 1
      assign env2_lrow = env2_lrow[1] | split: '|' | first
      assign env2_skey = ',' | append: env2_slot | append: '='
      assign env2_hit = env2_lrow | split: env2_skey
      if env2_hit.size > 1
        assign env2_i = env2_hit[1] | split: ',' | first | plus: 0
      endif
    endif
  endif
  assign env2_fb = fallback | default: -1 | plus: 0
  if env2_i < 0 and env2_fb >= 0
    assign env2_i = env2_fb
  endif
  if env2_i < 0
    # catalogue defaults for every other product: a context slot wants a scene, a close slot the next frame
    assign env2_i = 0
    if env2_slot == 'close' or env2_slot == 'small' or env2_slot == 'wall-pair' or env2_slot == 'ask'
      assign env2_i = 1
    endif
  endif
  if env2_i >= env2_n
    assign env2_i = 0
  endif

  # 2. the never-use guard: step to the first allowed index, wrapping
  assign env2_bad = ''
  assign env2_dhit = env2_deny | split: '|'
  for env2_row in env2_dhit
    assign env2_pair = env2_row | split: '='
    if env2_pair.size > 1 and env2_pair[0] == product.handle
      assign env2_bad = env2_pair[1]
    endif
  endfor
  if env2_bad != ''
    assign env2_probe = ',' | append: env2_i | append: ','
    if env2_bad contains env2_probe
      assign env2_found = -1
      for env2_step in (1..12)
        if env2_found < 0
          assign env2_try = env2_i | plus: env2_step | modulo: env2_n
          assign env2_probe2 = ',' | append: env2_try | append: ','
          unless env2_bad contains env2_probe2
            assign env2_found = env2_try
          endunless
        endif
      endfor
      if env2_found >= 0
        assign env2_i = env2_found
      endif
    endif
  endif
  echo env2_i
-%}
{%- endif -%}
